---- Reflect.construct(C, [5])
as it stands => ('C', [('x', 5)]) THEN ('C', [('x', 5)])
another __init__ => ('C', [('x', 5)]) THEN ('C', [('other', 5)])
another in the base => ('C', [('x', 5)]) THEN ('C', [('other', 5)])
none => ('C', [('x', 5)]) THEN TypeError: C() takes no arguments
a __new__ => ('C', [('x', 5)]) THEN made otherwise
one that returns something => ('C', [('x', 5)]) THEN TypeError: __init__() should return None, not 'int'
one that raises => ('C', [('x', 5)]) THEN ZeroDivisionError: division by zero
---- with nothing to be given
as it stands => ('C', []) THEN ('C', [])
an __init__ => ('C', []) THEN ('C', [('other', 0)])
given something all the same => TypeError: C() takes no arguments THEN ('C', [('other', 1)])
---- of which nothing is kept
nothing is made of it => 4999 THEN ZeroDivisionError: division by zero
only what it has => 4999 THEN None
